#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
spec2thunk -- generate an AMD64 "Wine builtin" thunk PE DLL.

The generated DLL is never executed by the host CPU; it exists so that an
x86-64 Windows PE guest can bind its imports to AMD64 code at a known,
tabulated address.  A host-side dispatcher maps a trapping RIP back to an
export index using the exported __wine_thunk_info structure:

    struct {
        uint32_t version;    /* = 4 */
        uint32_t count;
        uint32_t stubs_rva;
        uint32_t stride;     /* = 16 */
        uint32_t names_rva;  /* count x uint32 RVA -> NUL-terminated name  */
        uint32_t sigs_rva;   /* count x uint32 signature descriptor        */
        uint32_t trap_off;   /* byte offset of the trapping instruction
                                within a stub: 3 for trap, 0 for direct    */
        uint32_t impl_names_rva; /* count x uint32 RVA -> the name to resolve
                                in the NATIVE module.  The same string as
                                names_rva[i] except for a variadic, where it
                                is the v-variant -- see below.             */
    };

Version 4 appended impl_names_rva; the first seven fields keep their v3
offsets, so a v3 reader that stops after trap_off still reads the same bytes.

A trapping RIP is stubs_rva + index*stride + trap_off -- NOT a clean multiple
of the stride -- so the dispatcher can both recover the index and confirm the
trap landed exactly on a published trap site.

GUEST ARGUMENT REGISTERS AT THE TRAP.  x86-64 SYSCALL architecturally writes
the address of the following instruction into RCX and RFLAGS into R11.  RCX is
MS-x64's FIRST argument register, so a bare `0f 05` stub destroys arg0 before
the host can see it.  The trap stub therefore rescues it first:

        49 89 ca    mov r10, rcx      ; arg0 out of the way
        0f 05       syscall           ; now free to clobber rcx/r11

which puts the host-visible argument registers at:

        arg0 -> R10 (rescued from RCX)   arg1 -> RDX
        arg2 -> R8                       arg3 -> R9
        arg4+ -> [RSP + 8 + i*8]  (past the return address and the 32-byte
                                   shadow space)

Signature descriptor bits:
    0..7    number of integer/pointer arguments (0..16).  For a VARIADIC this
            is the number of FIXED arguments, i.e. where the `...` begins.
    8       set if the function returns void
    9       VARIADIC -- see below
    10..31  reserved, always 0

SIGNATURES COME FROM WINE'S HEADERS, NOT FROM THE SPEC FILE.  The spec file's
nargs / return-kind / header:line columns are ASSERTIONS: they are checked
against what clang reads out of Wine's real headers (see wine_sig.py) and any
mismatch is a hard failure.  A function whose shape is not representable --
float or vector arguments, struct by value, a return wider than 64 bits, or no
declaration at all -- is REFUSED and listed, never described with a
plausible-looking descriptor.

A va_list ARGUMENT IS NOT REFUSED on this ABI pair -- it is one pointer-sized
slot on both sides, measured, not assumed.  See the long note in wine_sig.py
before changing that back.

TRUE `...` VARIADICS ARE SUPPORTED, VIA THE CALLEE'S OWN v-VARIANT.  A
fixed-arity stub cannot forward `...` -- it cannot know the argument count.
It does not have to: it never calls the variadic function at all.  The host
calls that function's v-variant (printf -> vprintf, _snprintf -> _vsnprintf),
handing it a va_list synthesised from the guest's argument frame starting at
slot nfixed.  That is sound only because ppc64le ELFv2 va_list is a plain
pointer into a flat 8-byte-slot parameter save area, structurally identical to
MS-x64's -- measured end to end on the AC922, a guest-built MS-x64 va_list
consumed correctly by native ppc64 _vsnprintf ("%d-%s-%d" -> "4242-AB-77").
The sibling project ~/Development/powerpc64le-ports/wine-spec-thunk refuses
va_list outright; that refusal is about a different boundary and must not be
copied back here.  impl_names_rva[i] is what carries the v-variant name to the
host, and the generator REFUSES rather than guesses: the .thunks line must
name the v-variant, clang must agree the export really is variadic, and the
oracle must confirm nargs(v-variant) == nfixed + 1.  Nothing is derived by
string munging the export name.

Spec file format (see kernel32.thunks):
    DLL   kernel32.dll
    <ExportName>  <imm32>  <nargs>  <int|void>  <header.h>:<line>
    <ExportName>  <imm32>  <nfixed> <int|void>  <header.h>:<line>  variadic=<impl>
Export order in the file IS the stub index order.  The optional sixth token is
the ONLY way to describe a variadic; five tokens keep their exact old meaning.

The location column may name a Wine `.spec` file instead of a header, for the
handful of exports Wine implements in C and exports from a .spec but declares
in NO header (kernel32's delay-load entry points).  That path is a deliberate
downgrade: a .spec pins the arity and the argument classes but carries no
return type, so the <int|void> column becomes an unchecked human assertion and
the entry is listed under a loud banner at generation time.  Use a header
whenever one exists.

BUILDING.  A module with a <name>.thunks file beside its <name>.spec gets an
x86_64-windows/<name>.dll target, and "make" produces it like any other PE
module -- see output_source_thunks() in tools/makedep.c.  "make install" puts
it in $(libdir)/wine/x86_64-windows, which is already where the loader looks
for a builtin of that machine, so nothing needs staging into a prefix by hand.

RUNNING IT DIRECTLY, to regenerate or extend one module after Wine is built or
installed, without a full rebuild:

    tools/spec2thunk/spec2thunk --spec dlls/kernel32/kernel32.thunks \
        --body=trap --out <builddir>/dlls/kernel32/x86_64-windows/kernel32.dll

From the top of the build directory that is enough.  From anywhere else add
--wine-generated <builddir>/include: the widl-generated headers the signature
oracle needs are build output, not source, and the tool says so rather than
letting clang fail confusingly.

THE EXPORT LIST COMES FROM THE MODULE'S OWN WINE .spec.  A .thunks file used to
BE the list, plus an assertion about each signature.  But the list already
exists and nobody maintains it twice: winebuild turns <mod>.spec into the
module's real export table, so it IS, by construction, the set of names a guest
could import.

    spec2thunk --from-spec dlls/kernel32/kernel32.spec --body=trap --out ...

`@ stub` lines are skipped -- there is no implementation to call -- as are
entries this machine does not export at all (-arch=/-i386), -noname entries
(exported by ordinal, so there is no name to bind) and -register entries (which
take a CONTEXT, not an argument list).  Each of those is reported as a SKIP with
its reason, separately from the refusals, because they are not the same thing.

THE .spec SUPPLIES ONLY *WHICH NAMES EXIST*.  Every signature still comes from
clang reading Wine's real headers: a .spec has no return type at all and its
`long` is 32 bits.  What it does state exactly is the ARITY and the argument
CLASSES, and that is used as an independent CROSS-CHECK -- an export whose .spec
arity disagrees with its header declaration is refused and listed, never emitted
on one source's word.  (That check found two real Wine bugs the first time it
ran: kernel32.spec's RtlUnwindEx was one argument short of ntdll's, and
kernel32/kernelbase spelled VerSetConditionMask's ULONGLONG as two `long`s,
which is right on i386 and wrong on win64.  Both fixed.)

A .thunks FILE IS NOW UNNECESSARY, NOT FORBIDDEN.  A module with nothing to say
needs no file at all.  A module with a few things to say keeps a small one:

    DLL       kernel32.dll
    FROM-SPEC auto                  # or a path; `auto` = <mod>.spec beside it
    EXCLUDE   SomeExport            # drop one name
    DelayLoadFailureHook 0xD1A0 2 int kernel32.spec:366   # an OVERRIDE

With a FROM-SPEC line the export LINES become overrides for the handful of names
the .spec cannot describe -- a `variadic=<v-variant>` opt-in, a .spec location
for something Wine declares in no header, a deliberate arity/return assertion --
and everything else comes from the .spec.  Without one, the file means exactly
what it always meant, which is why the five hand-written modules still build
byte-for-byte identically.

REFUSALS ARE NORMAL AT THIS SCALE AND ARE NOT ERRORS.  A whole kernel32.spec
emits about 87% of its eligible exports; the rest are refused, biggest reason
first, with `--report FILE` giving the per-export detail as TSV.  --strict still
turns any refusal into a failure for a module that expects none.

"""

import argparse
import os
import shutil
import tempfile
import re
import struct
import subprocess
import sys
import time

import wine_sig
from wine_sig import Refused

STRIDE = 16
INFO_VERSION = 4
# Byte offset of the trapping instruction inside a stub, per body mode.
TRAP_OFF = {'direct': 0, 'trap': 3}
BUILTIN_SIG = b"Wine builtin DLL\x00"   # 17 bytes, must sit at file offset 0x40
SIG_OFF = 0x40
IMAGE_BASE = 0x180000000


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# spec file
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

def parse_spec(path):
    """Read a .thunks file -> (dll, exports, from_spec, excludes).

    TWO ROLES, AND THE FILE SAYS WHICH.  Without a FROM-SPEC line the export
    lines ARE the list, exactly as they always were.  With one, the list comes
    from the module's own Wine .spec and the export lines become OVERRIDES for
    the handful of names that need something the .spec cannot say -- a
    `variadic=<v-variant>` opt-in, a .spec location for a name Wine declares in
    no header, or a deliberate arity/return assertion.  EXCLUDE drops a name.

    So a .thunks file becomes UNNECESSARY rather than forbidden: a module with
    nothing to override needs no file at all (--from-spec on the command line),
    one with a few needs only those lines, and the five hand-written ones keep
    working untouched.
    """
    dll = None
    from_spec = None
    excludes = []
    exports = []          # (name, imm32, nargs, returns_void, header, line)
    with open(path) as f:
        for lineno, raw in enumerate(f, 1):
            line = raw.split('#', 1)[0].strip()
            if not line:
                continue
            parts = line.split()
            if parts[0].upper() == 'DLL':
                if len(parts) != 2:
                    sys.exit("%s:%d: DLL needs exactly one argument" % (path, lineno))
                dll = parts[1]
                continue
            if parts[0].upper() == 'FROM-SPEC':
                if len(parts) != 2:
                    sys.exit("%s:%d: FROM-SPEC needs exactly one argument: the "
                             "module's .spec, or 'auto' to look for "
                             "<name>.spec beside this file" % (path, lineno))
                if from_spec is not None:
                    sys.exit("%s:%d: a second FROM-SPEC line" % (path, lineno))
                from_spec = parts[1]
                continue
            if parts[0].upper() == 'EXCLUDE':
                if len(parts) != 2:
                    sys.exit("%s:%d: EXCLUDE needs exactly one export name"
                             % (path, lineno))
                excludes.append(parts[1])
                continue
            if len(parts) not in (5, 6):
                sys.exit("%s:%d: expected "
                         "'<Name> <imm32> <nargs> <int|void> <header.h>:<line>"
                         "[ variadic=<impl>]'" % (path, lineno))
            name, imm, nargs, retkind, loc = parts[:5]
            # Sixth token, optional: variadic=<name to resolve natively>.
            # Five tokens means exactly what it always meant.
            variadic_impl = None
            if len(parts) == 6:
                tok = parts[5]
                if not tok.startswith('variadic='):
                    sys.exit("%s:%d: unknown 6th token %r; the only one "
                             "defined is 'variadic=<impl>'" % (path, lineno, tok))
                variadic_impl = tok[len('variadic='):]
                if not variadic_impl:
                    sys.exit("%s:%d: variadic= needs the name of the "
                             "v-variant to call, e.g. variadic=vprintf"
                             % (path, lineno))
                if variadic_impl == name:
                    sys.exit("%s:%d: variadic=%s names the variadic export "
                             "itself; it must name that function's v-variant"
                             % (path, lineno, variadic_impl))
                if loc.endswith('.spec') or '.spec:' in loc:
                    sys.exit("%s:%d: variadic= requires a header location; a "
                             "Wine .spec carries no return type and its "
                             "`@ varargs` line lists only the fixed arguments, "
                             "so the v-variant cross-check is impossible"
                             % (path, lineno))
            try:
                imm = int(imm, 0)
                nargs = int(nargs, 0)
            except ValueError:
                sys.exit("%s:%d: bad number" % (path, lineno))
            if not (0 <= imm <= 0xffffffff):
                sys.exit("%s:%d: imm32 out of range" % (path, lineno))
            if retkind not in ('int', 'void'):
                sys.exit("%s:%d: return kind must be 'int' or 'void'" % (path, lineno))
            if ':' not in loc:
                sys.exit("%s:%d: location must be <header.h>:<line>" % (path, lineno))
            hdr, _, ln = loc.rpartition(':')
            try:
                ln = int(ln)
            except ValueError:
                sys.exit("%s:%d: bad line number in %r" % (path, lineno, loc))
            exports.append(dict(name=name, imm=imm, nargs=nargs,
                                returns_void=(retkind == 'void'),
                                header=hdr, line=ln,
                                variadic_impl=variadic_impl,
                                asserted=True,
                                specline=lineno))
    if dll is None:
        sys.exit("%s: no 'DLL <name>' line" % path)
    if not exports and from_spec is None:
        sys.exit("%s: no exports" % path)
    names = [e['name'] for e in exports]
    if len(set(names)) != len(names):
        sys.exit("%s: duplicate export names" % path)
    if '__wine_thunk_info' in names:
        sys.exit("%s: __wine_thunk_info is reserved" % path)
    return dll, exports, from_spec, excludes


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE EXPORT LIST, DERIVED FROM THE MODULE'S OWN WINE .spec
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The .spec is the list nobody maintains twice: it is what winebuild turns into
# the module's real export table, so it is by construction the set of names a
# guest could import.  It supplies ONLY WHICH NAMES EXIST.  Every signature
# still comes from clang reading Wine's real headers -- a .spec has no return
# type at all and its `long` is 32 bits, so it cannot describe a thunk (see the
# banner at the top of wine_sig.py).
#
# What the .spec DOES state exactly is the arity and the CLASS of each
# argument, and that is used here as an independent CROSS-CHECK of what clang
# read, not as a source: an export whose .spec arity disagrees with its header
# declaration is refused and listed, never emitted on one source's word.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# tools/tools.h get_cpu_from_name(), which matches by PREFIX: the table entry
# has to be a prefix of the spelling in the file, so "x86_64" matches and a
# bare "x86" matches nothing.
_CPU_NAMES = (('i386', 'i386'), ('i486', 'i386'), ('i586', 'i386'),
              ('i686', 'i386'), ('i786', 'i386'), ('x86_64', 'x86_64'),
              ('amd64', 'x86_64'), ('aarch64', 'arm64'), ('arm64ec', 'arm64ec'),
              ('arm64', 'arm64'), ('arm', 'arm'), ('ppc64', 'powerpc64'),
              ('powerpc64', 'powerpc64'))
# tools/winebuild/build.h FLAG_CPU_WIN32 / FLAG_CPU_WIN64.
_CPU_WIN32 = frozenset(('i386', 'arm'))
_CPU_WIN64 = frozenset(('x86_64', 'arm64', 'arm64ec', 'powerpc64'))
_CPU_ALL = _CPU_WIN32 | _CPU_WIN64
# The machine the generated thunk PE is for.  Not configurable: the whole file
# is an AMD64 PE by construction (IMAGE_FILE_MACHINE_AMD64, MS-x64 stubs).
GUEST_CPU = 'x86_64'

# .spec entry types that are a callable function with an argument list.
_SPEC_FUNC_TYPES = frozenset(('stdcall', 'cdecl', 'varargs', 'thiscall',
                              'fastcall'))


def _cpu_from_name(tok):
    for prefix, cpu in _CPU_NAMES:
        if tok.startswith(prefix):
            return cpu
    return None


def _spec_cpus(flags):
    """-> set of CPUs an entry is exported for, or None for "all of them".

    Reimplements tools/winebuild/parser.c parse_spec_flags()'s -arch= handling
    and its `-i386` backwards-compatibility alias, including the `!cpu`
    negation and the "x86-64 implies arm64ec" rule.
    """
    cpus, mask = set(), set()
    for f in flags:
        if f == 'i386':                        # backwards compatibility
            cpus.add('i386')
        elif f.startswith('arch='):
            for tok in f[len('arch='):].split(','):
                if tok == 'win32':
                    cpus |= _CPU_WIN32
                elif tok == 'win64':
                    cpus |= _CPU_WIN64
                else:
                    neg = tok.startswith('!')
                    cpu = _cpu_from_name(tok[1:] if neg else tok)
                    if cpu is None:
                        raise SystemExit("unknown architecture %r in -%s"
                                         % (tok, f))
                    (mask if neg else cpus).add(cpu)
    if 'x86_64' in cpus:
        cpus.add('arm64ec')
    if 'x86_64' in mask:
        mask.add('arm64ec')
    if mask:
        cpus |= _CPU_ALL - mask
    return cpus or None


def parse_wine_spec(path):
    """Read a Wine .spec -> (ordered entries, skipped-with-reason).

    An entry is dict(name, spec_args, spec_type, flags, specline).  `spec_args`
    is the argument-type list exactly as the .spec spells it, kept for the
    arity/class cross-check; it is never the source of a signature.

    Everything the guest cannot bind to a named AMD64 export is skipped here
    rather than refused later, with the reason, so the two are not confused in
    the report: a `@ stub` has no implementation to call at all, and an
    -arch-restricted entry is simply not in this machine's export table.
    """
    entries, skipped = [], []
    with open(path, errors='replace') as f:
        for lineno, raw in enumerate(f, 1):
            line = raw.split('#', 1)[0].strip()
            if not line:
                continue
            parts = line.split()
            if len(parts) < 2:
                continue
            ordinal, kind, rest = parts[0], parts[1], parts[2:]
            if ordinal != '@' and not ordinal.isdigit():
                continue                       # not an export line at all
            flags = []
            while rest and rest[0].startswith('-'):
                flags.append(rest.pop(0)[1:])
            if kind == 'stub':
                name = rest[0].split('(')[0] if rest else '?'
                skipped.append((name, lineno, 'stub -- Wine has no '
                                'implementation to call'))
                continue
            if kind not in _SPEC_FUNC_TYPES:
                # extern/variable/equate: data, not a callable entry point.
                if rest:
                    skipped.append((rest[0].split('(')[0], lineno,
                                    '`@ %s` is not a callable entry point' % kind))
                continue
            if not rest:
                continue
            decl = ' '.join(rest)
            name, _, tail = decl.partition('(')
            name = name.strip()
            args = tail.rpartition(')')[0].split() if '(' in decl else []
            cpus = _spec_cpus(flags)
            if cpus is not None and GUEST_CPU not in cpus:
                skipped.append((name, lineno,
                                'not exported for %s (-%s)'
                                % (GUEST_CPU,
                                   ' -'.join(f for f in flags
                                             if f == 'i386' or f.startswith('arch=')))))
                continue
            if name == '@':
                # `86 stdcall -i386 -private @(ptr) krnl386...`: exported by
                # ordinal under no name at all.
                skipped.append((name, lineno, '-noname: exported by ordinal '
                                'only, so there is no name to bind'))
                continue
            if not name.replace('_', 'a').replace('.', 'a').isalnum():
                skipped.append((name, lineno, 'name is not a plain C identifier'))
                continue
            if 'noname' in flags:
                # winebuild puts no name in the export table for these; a guest
                # can only reach them by ordinal, which a thunk PE built from
                # names cannot serve.
                skipped.append((name, lineno, '-noname: exported by ordinal '
                                'only, so there is no name to bind'))
                continue
            if 'register' in flags:
                skipped.append((name, lineno, '-register: the entry point takes '
                                'a CONTEXT, not an argument list'))
                continue
            entries.append(dict(name=name, spec_args=args, spec_type=kind,
                                flags=flags, specline=lineno))
    if not entries:
        sys.exit('%s: no usable export lines' % path)
    return entries, skipped


def exports_from_wine_spec(path, overrides=None, excludes=(), start_imm=0):
    """-> (export entries in .spec order, skipped, dropped-by-EXCLUDE).

    `overrides` maps an export name to a parsed .thunks line, which then
    supplies the assertion columns (and `variadic=`) for that one export
    exactly as it does in --spec mode.  Anything not overridden carries
    asserted=False and is checked against the .spec's own arity instead.
    """
    overrides = overrides or {}
    entries, skipped = parse_wine_spec(path)
    excluded = set(excludes)
    out, dropped = [], []
    for e in entries:
        if e['name'] in excluded:
            dropped.append(e['name'])
            continue
        ov = overrides.get(e['name'])
        if ov:
            e = dict(ov, spec_args=e['spec_args'], spec_type=e['spec_type'],
                     specline=e['specline'], asserted=True)
        else:
            # No hand-written assertion to check: the header oracle is the only
            # source, cross-checked against this line's own arity.  imm is only
            # read by --body=direct, where it just has to be distinct per stub.
            e = dict(e, imm=start_imm + len(out), nargs=None,
                     returns_void=None, header=None, line=None,
                     variadic_impl=None, asserted=False)
        e['imm'] = e.get('imm', start_imm + len(out))
        out.append(e)
    unknown = sorted(set(overrides) - {e['name'] for e in entries})
    if unknown:
        skipped_names = {n: why for n, _l, why in skipped}
        sys.exit('%s: %d override(s) name an export this .spec does not offer:\n  '
                 % (path, len(unknown))
                 + '\n  '.join('%-30s %s' % (n, skipped_names.get(
                     n, 'no such line in the .spec at all'))
                     for n in unknown))
    return out, skipped, dropped


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# signature resolution against Wine's headers
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

def resolve_signatures(exports, headers, specs=None):
    """-> (accepted, refused).  Hard-fails on a spec/header disagreement.

    The location column normally names a Wine HEADER, and that entry is fully
    verified by clang.  If it names a Wine `.spec` file instead, the entry
    takes the last-resort arity oracle (wine_sig.WineSpecs) -- read the class
    docstring, in particular that its <int|void> column is an UNCHECKED human
    assertion.  Those entries are collected and reported separately.

    AN ENTRY WITH asserted=False CAME FROM A WINE .spec, NOT FROM A HAND-WRITTEN
    LINE, so there is no nargs / int|void / header:line claim to police.  The
    .spec's OWN argument list is used as the cross-check instead: a disagreement
    between it and the header declaration is a REFUSAL of that one export, not a
    fatal error for the module.  A hand-written line is a promise somebody made
    and a broken one is a bug; a whole-.spec run legitimately meets exports Wine
    describes inconsistently, and killing the build over each is useless.
    """
    # ONE clang run for the whole module's stage-2 probes instead of one per
    # export.  This decides nothing on its own -- see WineHeaders.prefetch():
    # a clean batch memoises acceptances, anything a diagnostic touches still
    # takes its own single-symbol probe and its own message.  Ask for the
    # v-variants too, since every variadic makes a second signature() call.
    headers.prefetch(
        [(e['name'], e.get('variadic_impl') is not None)
         for e in exports if not (e['header'] or '').endswith('.spec')]
        + [(e['variadic_impl'], False)
           for e in exports if e.get('variadic_impl')])

    accepted, refused, mismatches = [], [], []
    for e in exports:
        want_variadic = e.get('variadic_impl') is not None
        # A .spec states the CLASS of each argument exactly, and that is one
        # thing it is authoritative about.  Refuse on it before spending a
        # header lookup, so the reason names the .spec that said so.
        bad = [a for a in (e.get('spec_args') or [])
               if a in wine_sig.WineSpecs.BAD_ARGS]
        if bad and not e.get('asserted', True):
            refused.append((e['name'], '%s (%s:%d)'
                            % (wine_sig.WineSpecs.BAD_ARGS[bad[0]],
                               os.path.basename(e.get('spec_path', '.spec')),
                               e['specline'])))
            continue
        try:
            if (e['header'] or '').endswith('.spec'):
                if specs is None:
                    raise Refused('.spec location cited but no source tree given')
                sig = specs.signature(e['name'], e['header'], e['line'],
                                      e['returns_void'])
            else:
                sig = headers.signature(e['name'],
                                        allow_variadic=want_variadic)
        except Refused as ex:
            refused.append((e['name'], ex.reason))
            continue
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------
        # variadic= is an ASSERTION like every other column, and it is checked
        # in BOTH directions.  A variadic with no variadic= never gets here at
        # all -- allow_variadic stayed False and wine_sig refused it -- so the
        # only direction left to police is a variadic= on something that is not
        # in fact variadic, which would make the host synthesise a va_list out
        # of whatever happened to follow the last real argument.
        # ------------------------------------------------------------------
        if want_variadic and not sig.get('variadic'):
            mismatches.append(
                "%s: spec says variadic=%s, but %s:%s declares it NON-variadic"
                "  [%s]" % (e['name'], e['variadic_impl'], sig['header'],
                            sig['line'], sig['qualtype']))
        elif want_variadic:
            # Confirm the v-variant the SPEC named -- never derive it by string
            # munging the export name.  va_list is one ordinary pointer
            # parameter to the oracle, so the v-variant must have exactly one
            # argument more than the variadic has fixed arguments.
            try:
                impl = headers.signature(e['variadic_impl'])
            except Refused as ex:
                mismatches.append("%s: variadic=%s does not resolve: %s"
                                  % (e['name'], e['variadic_impl'], ex.reason))
            else:
                if impl['nargs'] != sig['nargs'] + 1:
                    mismatches.append(
                        "%s: variadic=%s pairing is wrong -- %d fixed args + "
                        "va_list needs %d, but the v-variant takes %d\n"
                        "      %-14s %s  (%s:%s)\n"
                        "      %-14s %s  (%s:%s)"
                        % (e['name'], e['variadic_impl'], sig['nargs'],
                           sig['nargs'] + 1, impl['nargs'],
                           e['name'], sig['qualtype'], sig['header'], sig['line'],
                           e['variadic_impl'], impl['qualtype'],
                           impl['header'], impl['line']))
                elif impl['returns_void'] != sig['returns_void']:
                    mismatches.append(
                        "%s: variadic=%s returns %s but %s returns %s; the "
                        "host returns the v-variant's value as the export's"
                        % (e['name'], e['variadic_impl'],
                           'void' if impl['returns_void'] else 'a value',
                           e['name'],
                           'void' if sig['returns_void'] else 'a value'))
                e['impl_sig'] = impl
        if e.get('asserted', True):
            # The spec's numbers are claims. Wine's headers are the fact.
            if sig['nargs'] != e['nargs']:
                mismatches.append("%s: spec says %d args, %s:%s says %d  [%s]"
                                  % (e['name'], e['nargs'], sig['header'],
                                     sig['line'], sig['nargs'], sig['qualtype']))
            if sig['returns_void'] != e['returns_void']:
                mismatches.append("%s: spec says returns %s, %s:%s says %s  [%s]"
                                  % (e['name'],
                                     'void' if e['returns_void'] else 'int',
                                     sig['header'], sig['line'],
                                     'void' if sig['returns_void'] else 'int',
                                     sig['qualtype']))
            if (sig['header'] != e['header']) or (sig['line'] != e['line']):
                mismatches.append("%s: spec cites %s:%d, clang found it at %s:%s"
                                  % (e['name'], e['header'], e['line'],
                                     sig['header'], sig['line']))
        elif e.get('spec_args') is not None:
            # Derived from a Wine .spec: cross-check clang against the .spec's
            # own argument list.  Two independent readings of the same module
            # have to agree about how many arguments it takes before we publish
            # a descriptor that tells the host how many to marshal.
            if sig['nargs'] != len(e['spec_args']):
                refused.append(
                    (e['name'],
                     "arity disagreement: %s:%d says %d arg(s) (%s), %s:%s says "
                     "%d  [%s]"
                     % (os.path.basename(e.get('spec_path', '.spec')),
                        e['specline'], len(e['spec_args']),
                        ' '.join(e['spec_args']) or 'none',
                        sig['header'], sig['line'], sig['nargs'],
                        sig['qualtype'])))
                continue
        e = dict(e)
        e['sig'] = sig
        e['desc'] = wine_sig.descriptor(sig)
        # What the host resolves in the NATIVE module.  Identical to the export
        # name for everything except a variadic, which forwards to the
        # v-variant the spec named.
        e['impl'] = e.get('variadic_impl') or e['name']
        accepted.append(e)
    if mismatches:
        sys.exit("FATAL: spec disagrees with Wine's headers:\n  "
                 + "\n  ".join(mismatches))
    return accepted, refused


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# grouping refusals for the report
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A whole .spec refuses hundreds of exports and the useful question is not
# "which ones" -- that is what --report is for -- but "how many, and for what".
# These turn one refusal's message, which names the offending type or export,
# into the CLASS of reason, so the histogram counts causes and not spellings.
# Nothing here decides anything: the refusal has already happened, with the
# compiler's own words, and that text is what goes in the report file.

_REFUSAL_CLASSES = (
    (r'^no declaration found in Wine headers$',
     'no declaration in any Wine header'),
    (r'is not integer/pointer class',
     'argument or return is not integer/pointer class '
     '(struct by value, float, vector)'),
    (r'is wider than 64 bits',
     'argument or return is wider than 64 bits'),
    (r'^varargs ',                       'variadic with no variadic=<v-variant>'),
    (r'^conflicting declarations',       'Wine declares it more than one way'),
    (r'^arity disagreement',             '.spec and header disagree on the argument count'),
    (r'^incompatible pointer types|^initialization of|initializing .* with an '
     r'expression of (incompatible )?type',
     'header prototype does not match the export (reconstruction rejected)'),
    (r'\bdouble argument\b|\bfloat argument\b',
     '.spec declares a float/double argument'),
    (r'\bint128 argument\b',             '.spec declares an int128 argument'),
    (r'descriptor field holds at most 16|host marshaller passes',
     'more arguments than the descriptor or the host marshaller can carry'),
    (r'variadic with no fixed argument', 'variadic with no fixed argument'),
    (r'^unknown \.spec argument type',   'unknown .spec argument type'),
)

_SKIP_CLASSES = (
    (r'^stub ',                  '`@ stub` -- Wine has no implementation'),
    (r'^not exported for ',      'not exported for this machine (-arch=/-i386)'),
    (r'^-noname',                '-noname: no name in the export table'),
    (r'^-register',              '-register: takes a CONTEXT, not arguments'),
    (r'is not a callable entry point', 'data export, not a function'),
    (r'not a plain C identifier', 'name is not a plain C identifier'),
)


def _classify(text, table, fallback):
    for pat, label in table:
        if re.search(pat, text):
            return label
    return fallback


def refusal_class(why):
    return _classify(why, _REFUSAL_CLASSES, 'other (see --report)')


def skip_class(why):
    return _classify(why, _SKIP_CLASSES, 'other')


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# stub bodies
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

def stub_bytes(mode, imm):
    """Exactly STRIDE bytes of x86-64 for one stub slot."""
    if mode == 'direct':
        body = b'\xb8' + struct.pack('<I', imm) + b'\xc3'     # mov eax,imm32; ret
    elif mode == 'trap':
        # mov r10, rcx  -- SYSCALL clobbers RCX, which is MS-x64 arg0.
        body = b'\x49\x89\xca' + b'\x0f\x05'                 # mov r10,rcx; syscall
    else:
        raise ValueError(mode)
    assert len(body) <= STRIDE
    return body + b'\xcc' * (STRIDE - len(body))              # int3 padding


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# assembly / def emission
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

def emit_asm(dll, exports, mode):
    out = []
    a = out.append
    a('\t# generated by tools/spec2thunk -- do not edit')
    a('\t# dll=%s body=%s stride=%d info_version=%d trap_off=%d'
      % (dll, mode, STRIDE, INFO_VERSION, TRAP_OFF[mode]))
    a('')
    a('\t.section\t.thunk,"xr"')
    a('\t.balign\t%d' % STRIDE)
    a('wine_thunk_stubs:')
    for i, e in enumerate(exports):
        b = stub_bytes(mode, e['imm'])
        a('\t.globl\twine_thunk_stub_%d' % i)
        a('wine_thunk_stub_%d:\t\t# %s' % (i, e['name']))
        a('\t.byte\t' + ','.join('0x%02X' % c for c in b))
    a('wine_thunk_stubs_end:')
    a('')
    a('\t.section\t.rdata,"dr"')
    a('\t.balign\t8')
    a('\t.globl\twine_thunk_info')
    a('wine_thunk_info:')
    a('\t.long\t%d\t\t\t# version' % INFO_VERSION)
    a('\t.long\t%d\t\t\t# count' % len(exports))
    a('\t.long\twine_thunk_stub_0@IMGREL\t# stubs_rva')
    a('\t.long\t%d\t\t\t# stride' % STRIDE)
    a('\t.long\twine_thunk_namev@IMGREL\t# names_rva')
    a('\t.long\twine_thunk_sigv@IMGREL\t# sigs_rva')
    a('\t.long\t%d\t\t\t# trap_off' % TRAP_OFF[mode])
    a('\t.long\twine_thunk_implv@IMGREL\t# impl_names_rva  (version 4)')
    a('')
    a('\t.balign\t4')
    a('wine_thunk_namev:')
    for i in range(len(exports)):
        a('\t.long\twine_thunk_name_%d@IMGREL' % i)
    a('')
    a('\t# The name the host resolves in the NATIVE module.  Identical to')
    a('\t# names_rva[i] -- the same string, deliberately not a copy -- except')
    a('\t# for a variadic, which forwards to its own v-variant.')
    a('\t.balign\t4')
    a('wine_thunk_implv:')
    for i, e in enumerate(exports):
        if e['impl'] == e['name']:
            a('\t.long\twine_thunk_name_%d@IMGREL' % i)
        else:
            a('\t.long\twine_thunk_impl_%d@IMGREL\t# %s -> %s'
              % (i, e['name'], e['impl']))
    a('')
    a('\t.balign\t4')
    a('wine_thunk_sigv:')
    for i, e in enumerate(exports):
        s = e['sig']
        a('\t.long\t0x%08X\t# %d %-24s %d %sarg%s, returns %s  (%s:%s)%s'
          % (e['desc'], i, e['name'], s['nargs'],
             'fixed ' if s.get('variadic') else '',
             '' if s['nargs'] == 1 else 's',
             'void' if s['returns_void'] else s['ret'], s['header'], s['line'],
             (' VARIADIC -> %s' % e['impl']) if s.get('variadic') else ''))
    a('')
    for i, e in enumerate(exports):
        a('wine_thunk_name_%d:' % i)
        a('\t.asciz\t"%s"' % e['name'])
        if e['impl'] != e['name']:
            a('wine_thunk_impl_%d:' % i)
            a('\t.asciz\t"%s"' % e['impl'])
    a('')
    a('\t# One absolute 64-bit pointer so the linker is forced to emit a')
    a('\t# base relocation directory; Wine relocates this image.')
    a('\t.balign\t8')
    a('wine_thunk_self:')
    a('\t.quad\twine_thunk_info')
    a('')
    return '\n'.join(out) + '\n'


def emit_def(dll, exports):
    out = ['LIBRARY %s' % dll, 'EXPORTS']
    for i, e in enumerate(exports):
        out.append('    %s = wine_thunk_stub_%d' % (e['name'], i))
    out.append('    __wine_thunk_info = wine_thunk_info DATA')
    return '\n'.join(out) + '\n'


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# post-link patch: stamp the Wine builtin signature at file offset 0x40
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

def stamp_builtin_signature(path):
    with open(path, 'rb') as f:
        data = bytearray(f.read())
    if data[:2] != b'MZ':
        sys.exit("%s: not an MZ image" % path)
    e_lfanew = struct.unpack_from('<I', data, 0x3c)[0]
    end = SIG_OFF + len(BUILTIN_SIG)          # 0x51
    if e_lfanew <= end:
        sys.exit("FATAL: e_lfanew=0x%x <= 0x%x; stamping the builtin "
                 "signature would clobber the PE header. Refusing."
                 % (e_lfanew, end))
    if len(data) < 96:
        sys.exit("FATAL: image shorter than sizeof(IMAGE_DOS_HEADER)+32")
    data[SIG_OFF:end] = BUILTIN_SIG
    with open(path, 'wb') as f:
        f.write(data)
    return e_lfanew


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

def run(cmd, verbose):
    if verbose:
        print('+ ' + ' '.join(cmd), file=sys.stderr)
    r = subprocess.run(cmd)
    if r.returncode != 0:
        sys.exit("command failed (%d): %s" % (r.returncode, ' '.join(cmd)))


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()
    ap.add_argument('--spec', help='a .thunks file.  Without a FROM-SPEC line '
                                   'its export lines ARE the list; with one '
                                   'they are overrides for a list taken from '
                                   "the module's own Wine .spec")
    ap.add_argument('--from-spec', metavar='<mod>.spec',
                    help="derive the export list from the module's own Wine "
                         '.spec.  Signatures still come from clang reading '
                         "Wine's headers -- a .spec has no return type and its "
                         '`long` is 32 bits.  May be combined with --spec, in '
                         'which case the .thunks lines are overrides.')
    ap.add_argument('--dll-name', metavar='<name>.dll',
                    help='name for the generated DLL.  Defaults to the DLL line '
                         'of the .thunks file, or to the .spec basename')
    ap.add_argument('--report', metavar='FILE',
                    help='write the machine-readable per-export outcome '
                         '(name, verdict, reason) here, one TSV row each')
    ap.add_argument('--body', choices=('direct', 'trap'), required=True)
    # No default output location: a build tool writes where it is told.  The
    # old defaults pointed into one developer's /tmp and were pure scaffolding.
    ap.add_argument('--outdir', default=None,
                    help='directory for the generated DLL; --out overrides it')
    ap.add_argument('--builddir', default=None,
                    help='directory for intermediates; defaults to a temporary '
                         'one that is removed unless -v is given')
    ap.add_argument('--out', help='explicit output path (overrides --outdir)')
    ap.add_argument('--implib',
                    help='import library path; defaults to '
                         '<outdir>/<stem>.import.lib, which is deliberately '
                         'mode-independent -- the export names are identical '
                         'in direct and trap mode, so one implib serves both')
    ap.add_argument('--wine-include', default=wine_sig.DEFAULT_INCLUDE)
    ap.add_argument('--wine-generated', default=None,
                    help='directory holding the widl-generated headers; '
                         'defaults to ./include then the source include dir')
    ap.add_argument('--wine-source', default=wine_sig.DEFAULT_SOURCE,
                    help='Wine source root, used only to resolve a .spec '
                         'location column (last-resort arity oracle)')
    ap.add_argument('--strict', action='store_true',
                    help='treat any refused export as a fatal error')
    ap.add_argument('--clang', default='clang')
    ap.add_argument('--linker', default='lld-link')
    ap.add_argument('--crt-define', action='append', default=None,
                    metavar='-D...',
                    help='override the CRT-selection define(s) the header '
                         'oracle probes with.  By default these are derived '
                         'from the DLL line of the spec by Wine\'s own rule '
                         '(tools/makedep.c get_crt_define): ucrt* -> -D_UCRT, '
                         'msvcrt -> -D_MSVCR_VER=0, msvcr<N> -> '
                         '-D_MSVCR_VER=<N>, anything else -> nothing.  Pass '
                         'this only to probe a runtime other than the one the '
                         'spec names; an empty string means "no define".')
    ap.add_argument('-v', '--verbose', action='store_true')
    args = ap.parse_args()

    if not args.spec and not args.from_spec:
        ap.error('one of --spec <mod>.thunks or --from-spec <mod>.spec is '
                 'required')

    # ---------------- where the export list comes from
    dll, spec_exports, from_spec, excludes = None, [], None, []
    if args.spec:
        dll, spec_exports, from_spec, excludes = parse_spec(args.spec)
    if args.from_spec:
        from_spec = args.from_spec
    elif from_spec == 'auto':
        # `FROM-SPEC auto` = the .spec sitting beside this .thunks file, which
        # is where Wine keeps it.  Named rather than guessed at, so a module
        # that keeps it elsewhere can just say where.
        from_spec = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(args.spec)),
                                 os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(dll or
                                                                   args.spec))[0]
                                 + '.spec')
    elif from_spec and args.spec:
        # A relative FROM-SPEC is relative to the .thunks file that names it.
        if not os.path.isabs(from_spec):
            from_spec = os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(args.spec)),
                                     from_spec)

    wine_spec_skipped, wine_spec_dropped = [], []
    if from_spec:
        if not os.path.isfile(from_spec):
            ap.error('no such Wine .spec: %s' % from_spec)
        overrides = {e['name']: e for e in spec_exports}
        spec_exports, wine_spec_skipped, wine_spec_dropped = \
            exports_from_wine_spec(from_spec, overrides, excludes)
        for e in spec_exports:
            e.setdefault('spec_path', from_spec)
        if not dll:
            dll = os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(from_spec))[0] + '.dll'
    elif excludes:
        keep = set(excludes)
        wine_spec_dropped = [e['name'] for e in spec_exports if e['name'] in keep]
        spec_exports = [e for e in spec_exports if e['name'] not in keep]
    if args.dll_name:
        dll = args.dll_name
    if not spec_exports:
        sys.exit('no exports to emit')
    names = [e['name'] for e in spec_exports]
    if len(set(names)) != len(names):
        dup = sorted({n for n in names if names.count(n) > 1})
        sys.exit('duplicate export names: %s' % ', '.join(dup))
    if '__wine_thunk_info' in names:
        sys.exit('__wine_thunk_info is reserved')

    stem = os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(dll))[0]
    tmp_builddir = None
    if not args.builddir:
        tmp_builddir = args.builddir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='spec2thunk-')
    os.makedirs(args.builddir, exist_ok=True)

    # Wine's include/msvcrt/ headers describe several different C runtimes out
    # of one tree and default to UCRT's; reading msvcrt.dll's surface in that
    # default mode hides __getmainargs/__set_app_type and substitutes UCRT
    # inline forwarders for the real import declarations of vprintf/_vsnprintf.
    # See the crt_defines_for_dll() banner in wine_sig.py.
    crt_defines = ([d for d in args.crt_define if d]
                   if args.crt_define is not None
                   else wine_sig.crt_defines_for_dll(dll))

    if not args.wine_generated:
        args.wine_generated = wine_sig.find_generated_include()
        if not args.wine_generated:
            ap.error('cannot find the widl-generated headers (wtypes.h); run '
                     'from the top of the build directory or pass '
                     '--wine-generated <builddir>/include')
    headers = wine_sig.WineHeaders(args.wine_include, args.wine_generated,
                                   clang=args.clang,
                                   workdir=os.path.join(args.builddir, 'sigprobe'),
                                   defines=crt_defines)
    headers.sanity()
    specs = wine_sig.WineSpecs(args.wine_source)
    t0 = time.time()
    exports, refused = resolve_signatures(spec_exports, headers, specs)
    resolve_secs = time.time() - t0

    unverified = [e for e in exports if e['sig'].get('return_verified') is False]
    if unverified:
        print("!! RETURN KIND NOT VERIFIED -- Wine declares these in no header,")
        print("!! so arity came from the cited .spec line but the int/void")
        print("!! column below is a HUMAN ASSERTION taken from Wine's C source:")
        for e in unverified:
            print("  %-28s %-4s  %s:%d" % (e['name'],
                                           'void' if e['returns_void'] else 'int',
                                           e['sig']['header'], e['sig']['line']))
        print()

    if wine_spec_dropped:
        print("EXCLUDED BY THE .thunks FILE (%d): %s"
              % (len(wine_spec_dropped), ', '.join(sorted(wine_spec_dropped))))
        print()

    if refused:
        print("REFUSED EXPORTS (not emitted -- shape is not representable):")
        # Short lists stay verbatim, exactly as they always printed.  A whole
        # .spec produces hundreds, where a wall of lines hides the answer: what
        # the ceiling on this approach actually is.  So group by reason, biggest
        # first, and show examples -- the full per-export list goes to --report.
        if len(refused) <= 40:
            for name, why in refused:
                print("  %-28s %s" % (name, why))
        else:
            hist = {}
            for name, why in refused:
                hist.setdefault(refusal_class(why), []).append((name, why))
            for cls, rows in sorted(hist.items(), key=lambda kv: -len(kv[1])):
                print("  %5d  %.1f%%  %s"
                      % (len(rows), 100.0 * len(rows) / len(spec_exports), cls))
                for name, why in rows[:2]:
                    print("           e.g. %-26s %s" % (name, why[:150]))
        print()
        if args.strict:
            sys.exit("FATAL: --strict and %d export(s) refused" % len(refused))
    if not exports:
        sys.exit("FATAL: every export was refused; nothing to emit")

    if wine_spec_skipped or from_spec:
        print("EXPORT LIST  from %s" % (from_spec or args.spec))
        if wine_spec_skipped:
            hist = {}
            for _n, _l, why in wine_spec_skipped:
                hist.setdefault(skip_class(why), 0)
                hist[skip_class(why)] += 1
            print("  %5d  not eligible for an AMD64 thunk at all:"
                  % len(wine_spec_skipped))
            for cls, n in sorted(hist.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1]):
                print("         %5d  %s" % (n, cls))
        print("  %5d  eligible export(s) considered" % len(spec_exports))
        print("  %5d  emitted        (%.1f%% of eligible)"
              % (len(exports), 100.0 * len(exports) / len(spec_exports)))
        print("  %5d  refused        (%.1f%% of eligible)"
              % (len(refused), 100.0 * len(refused) / len(spec_exports)))
        print()

    if args.report:
        with open(args.report, 'w') as f:
            f.write('name\tverdict\tdetail\n')
            for n, l, why in wine_spec_skipped:
                f.write('%s\tskipped\t%s\n' % (n, why))
            for n in wine_spec_dropped:
                f.write('%s\texcluded\tEXCLUDE line in %s\n' % (n, args.spec))
            for e in exports:
                s = e['sig']
                f.write('%s\temitted\t%d args, %s, %s:%s\n'
                        % (e['name'], s['nargs'],
                           'void' if s['returns_void'] else 'value',
                           s['header'], s['line']))
            for n, why in refused:
                f.write('%s\trefused\t%s\n' % (n, why.replace('\t', ' ')))

    if not args.out and not args.outdir:
        ap.error('one of --out or --outdir is required')
    outpath = args.out or os.path.join(args.outdir, dll)
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(outpath), exist_ok=True)

    tag = '%s.%s' % (stem, args.body)
    spath = os.path.join(args.builddir, tag + '.s')
    opath = os.path.join(args.builddir, tag + '.o')
    dpath = os.path.join(args.builddir, tag + '.def')
    # Opt-in: "make" only wants the DLL, and an unrequested .import.lib beside
    # it is build-tree litter that nothing cleans.  Guest probes that link
    # against a thunk module ask for one explicitly.
    lpath = args.implib
    if lpath: os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(lpath)), exist_ok=True)

    with open(spath, 'w') as f:
        f.write(emit_asm(dll, exports, args.body))
    with open(dpath, 'w') as f:
        f.write(emit_def(dll, exports))

    run([args.clang, '-target', 'x86_64-windows-gnu', '-c', spath, '-o', opath],
        args.verbose)
    run([args.linker, '/dll', '/machine:x64', '/nodefaultlib', '/noentry',
         '/opt:noref', '/base:0x%x' % IMAGE_BASE, '/def:' + dpath,
         ('/implib:' + lpath) if lpath else '/noimplib',
         '/out:' + outpath, opath],
        args.verbose)

    e_lfanew = stamp_builtin_signature(outpath)

    print("dll          : %s" % dll)
    print("body mode    : %s" % args.body)
    print("crt mode     : %s" % (' '.join(crt_defines) if crt_defines
                                 else '(none -- not a C runtime module)'))
    print("info version : %d" % INFO_VERSION)
    print("output       : %s" % outpath)
    print("e_lfanew     : 0x%x (signature stamped at 0x%02x..0x%02x)"
          % (e_lfanew, SIG_OFF, SIG_OFF + len(BUILTIN_SIG) - 1))
    print("trap_off     : %d" % TRAP_OFF[args.body])
    print("import lib   : %s" % (lpath or "(none; pass --implib if you need one)"))
    st = headers.stats
    print("oracle       : %d clang run(s) for %d export(s) in %.1fs "
          "(%d AST dump%s indexing %d decls, %d probe compile%s: "
          "%d batched, %d one at a time)"
          % (st['ast_dumps'] + st['probe_compiles'], len(spec_exports),
             resolve_secs, st['ast_dumps'], '' if st['ast_dumps'] == 1 else 's',
             st['indexed_decls'], st['probe_compiles'],
             '' if st['probe_compiles'] == 1 else 's',
             st['batched_probes'], st['fallback_probes']))
    if tmp_builddir and not args.verbose:
        shutil.rmtree(tmp_builddir, ignore_errors=True)

    variadics = [e for e in exports if e['sig'].get('variadic')]
    if variadics:
        print()
        print("VARIADIC EXPORTS -- the host synthesises a va_list from the "
              "guest frame at")
        print("slot <fixed> and calls the impl below instead.  Both signatures "
              "clang-verified:")
        for e in variadics:
            s, im = e['sig'], e['impl_sig']
            print("  %-20s %d fixed  %s:%s  %s"
                  % (e['name'], s['nargs'], s['header'], s['line'], s['qualtype']))
            print("  %-20s -> impl  %s:%s  %s"
                  % ('', im['header'], im['line'], im['qualtype']))
        print()

    # A hand-written list is short enough to read; a whole .spec is 1300 rows of
    # scrollback that nobody reads and that buries the summary above it.  The
    # per-export detail is what --report exists for.
    if len(exports) > 250 and not args.verbose:
        print()
        print("(%d exports emitted; per-export table suppressed -- pass -v, or "
              "--report FILE)" % len(exports))
        return

    print("idx  export                     imm32       desc    args ret   "
          "impl                       from")
    for i, e in enumerate(exports):
        s = e['sig']
        print("%3d  %-26s 0x%08X  0x%05X %4d %-5s %-26s %s:%s"
              % (i, e['name'], e['imm'], e['desc'], s['nargs'],
                 'void' if s['returns_void'] else 'int',
                 e['impl'] + (' (V)' if s.get('variadic') else ''),
                 s['header'], s['line']))


if __name__ == '__main__':
    main()
